      ⍝ empty axis needed ----------------------------------

      T←⊂¨'ONE' 'FOUR' 'THREE'
      ≡¨T
2 2 2
      ⊃[ι0]T
 ONE FOUR THREE 

      ⍝ regression: X validation used to be an ad-hoc duplicate-only check
      ⍝ that (a) invoked undefined behaviour (1 << negative) for an axis
      ⍝ too small for the current ⎕IO, and (b) mislabeled any out-of-range
      ⍝ axis as a generic "Bad length of X" RANK ERROR instead of naming
      ⍝ the offending axis. Now reuses cValue::to_bitmap(), which reports
      ⍝ a proper AXIS ERROR naming the axis (and, when relevant, notes an
      ⍝ ⎕IO=0 dependency).
      ⍝
      ⊃[5]2 3⍴⍳6
AXIS ERROR+
      ⊃[5]2 3⍴⍳6
      ^
      )MORE
⊃[X]B: X[1] = 5 is not a valid axis (expecting 1≤X[1]<3).
      )SIC

      ⊃[1 1]2 3⍴⍳6
AXIS ERROR+
      ⊃[1 1]2 3⍴⍳6
      ^
      )MORE
⊃[X]B: X[2] = 1 is a duplicate axis.
      )SIC

      ⎕IO←0
      ⊃[2]2 3⍴⍳6
AXIS ERROR+
      ⊃[2]2 3⍴⍳6
      ^
      )MORE
⊃[X]B: X[0] = 2 is not a valid axis (expecting 0≤X[0]<2). Note: ⎕IO=0.
      )SIC

      ⎕IO←1

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #63, 2026-08-11): ⊃[X]B never
      ⍝ checked that ⍴,X matches the rank of the items of B -- to_bitmap()
      ⍝ above only rejects an axis out of range for cB (⊃B's own rank,
      ⍝ i.e. B's rank plus the items' rank), so too few or too many axes
      ⍝ in X, as long as they stayed within that wider range, silently
      ⍝ picked the wrong axes of cB instead of failing.
      ⍝
      ⊃[⍬](1 2)(3 4)             ⍝ items are rank 1, X has 0 items
AXIS ERROR+
      ⊃[⍬](1 2) (3 4)
      ^
      )MORE
⊃[X]B: ⍴,X (0) does not match the rank of the items of B (1)
      )SIC

      ⊃[1 2](1 2)(3 4)           ⍝ items are rank 1, X has 2 items
AXIS ERROR+
      ⊃[1 2](1 2) (3 4)
      ^
      )MORE
⊃[X]B: ⍴,X (2) does not match the rank of the items of B (1)
      )SIC

      M←2 3⍴⍳6 ⋄ ⍴⊃[1](⊂M),⊂M   ⍝ items are rank 2, X has 1 item
AXIS ERROR+
      ⍴⊃[1](⊂M),⊂M
       ^
      )MORE
⊃[X]B: ⍴,X (1) does not match the rank of the items of B (2)
      )SIC
      )ERASE M

      ⍝ control: X's length matching the items' rank still works
      ⍝
      ⊃[1](1 2)(3 4)
1 3
2 4
